        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(mattermost): truncate inbound preview on code-point boundary",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes garbled verbose inbound previews in Mattermost when message bodies contain emoji or other astral characters near the 200-character preview limit. Raw `slice(0, 200)` could split UTF-16 surrogate pairs, producing lone surrogates in gateway debug logs.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplaces `bodyText.slice(0, 200)` with `truncateUtf16Safe(bodyText, 200)` from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/text-utility-runtime` in the verbose inbound preview path.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators enabling verbose Mattermost inbound logging see clean previews on emoji boundaries. No change to message delivery or agent-visible content.\n\n## Evidence\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs run \\\n  extensions/mattermost/src/mattermost/monitor.inbound-system-event.test.ts \\\n  --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** Verbose inbound preview could split emoji astral characters at the 200-code-unit boundary.\n- **Real environment tested:** macOS (Darwin arm64), Node.js v22.22.0, local source checkout on branch `fix/mattermost-monitor-utf16-truncation`.\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:**\n  1. `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/mattermost/src/mattermost/monitor.inbound-system-event.test.ts --reporter=verbose`\n- **Evidence after fix:**\n\n```text\n ✓ keeps verbose inbound previews on complete UTF-16 boundaries\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  11 passed (11)\n```\n\n- **Observed result after fix:** A 199-ASCII + emoji + tail message produces preview `\"aaa…aaa\"` (199 `a` chars) with no split surrogate; verbose debug line matches production monitor path.\n- **What was not tested:** Live Mattermost websocket connection against a remote server.\n",
